
how to use:

	1. start the game by running python3 src/main.py in your terminal (make sure you have python installed)
	2. after clicking enter you can see a gameboard. there you see some letters below Hand:Player. each of those refers to the cards mentioned below. 
	3. pick a card by writing the letter and press enter to confirm. you can choose to Not play a card by writing 0. 
	4. if you've chosen a valid card it will ask you for the mode in which to play the card: D for direct or C for charged. 
		a) in this moment you can choose to enter B which brings you back into card selection
	5. if you've correctly entered the mode to play you will get be given the next option to play. 
	6. after going through the play phase you will see the reveal and the calculations. 
	7. keep on playing until you or the bot wins. it will be tricky though ;)
	8. you can always stop the program by pressing <ctrl> + <C>
	9. enjoy!



tables with card values:

	N - Novice Spell:
				attack		block		draw
		direct		1		1		0
		charged		2		2		1

	A - Academy Spell:
				attack		block		draw
		direct		2		2		1
		charged		4		3		2

	P - Professor's Spell:
				attack		block		draw
		direct		3		3		2
		charged		6		4		3

	F - The Forbidden Spell:
				attack		block		draw
		direct		0		0		B
		charged		4 LS		R		S


	LS ... lifesteal: any unblocked damage will be gained as health
	R ... reflects the damage back (including lifesteal) 
	B ... blocks the draw of the opponent (the amount of cards your opponent would draw from their cards)
	S ... steals the draw of the opponent (the amount of cards your opponent would draw from their cards)



special interactions:

	1. novice cannot be reflected by the forbidden spell (damage just goes through)
	2. if forbidden spell and novice are being revealed in the same turn both on their respective draw fields the following happens:
		- any effect of the forbidden spell is being ignored
		- the player with the novice draws one more card
	3. if the forbidden spell in charged mode is being reflected by the forbidden spell of your opponent: you will receive the damage from the forbidden spell (4) and your opponent will receive 	that much health



zero-card-rule:

	if a player has at the time of the reveal no cards in hand they will draw an extra card in the draw phase
		- if the players health is below 4 they instead draw two cards

